This function iterates through each character `char` in the input string `s`. If a character is an alphabet (either lower or uppercase), it flips the case. If the character is not an alphabet, it simply appends it to the resulting string unmodified. Importantly, this implementation treats non-letter characters (like numbers or special symbols) as is, which aligns with the requirement that they should not be flipped.
